The CSStransformproperty applies a 2D or 3D transformation to an element. This property allows 
you to rotate, scale, move, and skew elements.

Mouse over the elements below to see the difference between a 2D 
and a 3D transformation:

With the CSStransformproperty you can use 
the following 3D transformation functions:

TherotateX()function rotates an element around its X-axis at a given degree:

TherotateY()function rotates an element around its Y-axis at a given degree:

TherotateZ()function rotates an element around its Z-axis at a given degree:

The following table lists all the 3D transform properties:

### Code Snippets

```
#myDiv
{
transform: rotateX(150deg);
}

---

#myDiv
{
transform: rotateY(150deg);
}

---

#myDiv
{
transform: rotateZ(90deg);
}
```
